# Test: an internal ddos-detect whose interfaces receive nothing is reported blind by show doctor
# VALIDATES: the ddos-detect-rate-feed plugin doctor check end to end, on the
# real rate feed: the interface rate tracker (internal/component/iface/rate.go
# collect) reads the namespace's links, trafficstat (Service.tick) hands the
# rates to the detector (detector.go onRates, tickRates), observeFeed
# (blind.go) counts the zero run, and checkRateFeed (doctor.go) answers
# show doctor, the daemon form of ze doctor, through the plugin's own
# OnDoctorCheck callback. The fixture plugin
# (internal/test/fixture/ddos_detect_blind.go doctorDDoSDetectBlindZero) reads
# show doctor until doctor-ddos-detect-blind carries "has reported zero
# received packets and bytes", and returns an error otherwise. The WARN line
# observeFeed logs at the onset of the run is asserted too.
# PREVENTS: a detector that runs against zero traffic looking warmed and armed
# in ze doctor, with a ready baseline that can never trigger.
#
# The namespace is the precondition: the test needs a box with no received
# traffic, which a host or the shared guest root never is. option=netns-link
# makes the runner skip the test outside a namespace the QEMU launcher prepares:
# `./le test qemu netns suites plugin` (netnsSelections in
# internal/le/test/qemu/netns_linux.go names it) and a one-test
# `./le test qemu all test test/plugin/ddos-detect-internal-blind.ci` each run
# it in a fresh namespace holding lo and the dummy eth1. A dummy link receives
# nothing. lo carries only the fixture's own TLS connection to the daemon, so
# the fixture stays silent for longer than one window before each read
# (ddosBlindQuiet); it cannot poll, because a poll is received traffic.
#
# baseline-window 10 and check-interval 1 are the smallest values validation
# accepts (internal/plugins/ddos/detect/config.go), so the window is 10
# samples, one a second.
#
# needs-linux: ddos-detect depends on the interface plugin, which has no
# OS-default backend on darwin (see test/plugin/ddos-detect-external-warns.ci).

option=needs-linux
option=netns-link:name=eth1
# Serialize against every other ddos test, as
# test/plugin/ddos-detect-external-warns.ci does: rationale in
# test/plugin/ddos-direction.ci.
option=exclusive:group=ddos-flood
option=timeout:value=60s

stdin=ze-conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
ddos {
	detect {
		enabled true
		baseline-window 10
		check-interval 1
	}
}

plugin {
	external doctor-ddos-detect-blind-zero-test {
		run "le test fixture plugin/doctor-ddos-detect-blind-zero"
		encoder json
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-conf:timeout=60s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=OK: show doctor reports doctor-ddos-detect-blind for a detector that sees no traffic
expect=stderr:contains=has reported zero received packets and bytes on every interface for 10s
reject=stderr:pattern=panic
